# Database Skill

## Stack

* PostgreSQL
* SQLAlchemy ORM
* Alembic
* Async database access

## Database Architecture

Use layered database architecture:

```txt id="0txgmq"
models/
repositories/
services/
schemas/
```

## ORM Rules

* Use SQLAlchemy ORM
* Avoid raw SQL unless absolutely necessary
* Use typed ORM models
* Use relationships properly
* Avoid duplicated queries

## Repository Pattern

* All database access must go through repositories
* Routers must never query database directly
* Services should use repositories

## Query Rules

* Use pagination for large datasets
* Avoid N+1 queries
* Use joins carefully
* Select only required fields

## Transaction Rules

* Use transactions for critical operations
* Rollback on failure
* Keep transactions small

## Model Rules

* Use UUID or integer primary keys consistently
* Add created_at and updated_at timestamps
* Use soft delete when appropriate

## Migration Rules

* Use Alembic for migrations
* Never modify production tables manually
* Keep migrations atomic

## Performance Rules

* Add indexes for frequently queried columns
* Avoid loading unnecessary relationships
* Use lazy loading carefully

## Validation Rules

* Validate input before database operations
* Never trust frontend data
* Handle database exceptions gracefully

## Security Rules

* Never expose sensitive fields
* Never return password hashes
* Use parameterized queries
* Never concatenate SQL strings manually

## Example Folder Structure

```
backend/
 ├── app/
 │    ├── models/
 │    ├── repositories/
 │    ├── services/
 │    ├── schemas/
 │    └── db/
```

## Example Flow

```
Router
 -> Service
   -> Repository
      -> Database
```

## Anti-Patterns

Avoid:

* Business logic inside repositories
* Database queries inside routers
* Massive ORM models
* Returning ORM models directly to frontend
* Repeating query logic across services
